FINDING CORRECTION: drop poincare_distance from the import list, or route FrechetCodebook.distances through it as the module-level call.
FINDING SEVERITY: minor
FINDING LOCATION: model/layers.py:198-201
FINDING DETAIL: the curved KMeans initialisation assigns with frechet.distances(x, codebook) where x is the raw encoder output, whereas training and export always use point = clamp_ball(exp_0(latent)) (layers.py:153). The codebook is in the ball (layers.py:90-93) but the query point is not, so for a level-1 latent with norm above ~1 the artanh argument saturates at the 1-1e-7 clamp and the initial residual handed to the level-2/3 KMeans can differ from the training-time assignment. It stays finite (no inf/nan), is self-correcting after the first step, and touches only initialisation, not the estimator.
FINDING REPRODUCTION: compare layers.py:153 with layers.py:199-200; with a latent of norm 2 the mobius norm exceeds 1 and every distance collapses to 2*atanh(1-1e-7).
FINDING CORRECTION: use clamp_ball(exp_0(x)) in the initialisation too, e.g. self.frechet.distances(clamp_ball(exp_0(x)), self.get_code_embs()).

