EXERCISED PATH: model/layers.py:153-178 -> model/model.py:87-94 -> train_rqvae.py:441-447 -> model/frechet_poincare.py:159-199 -> train_rqvae.py:451-459 | Exercised by tracing the autograd graph term by term. commitment = self.frechet.commitment(point, code.detach()) (layers.py:176) with point = clamp_ball(exp_0(latent)) (layers.py:153) is differentiable in the encoder, so beta*(weights*commitment).mean() (layers.py:177) puts the successor weights directly into the encoder gradient; reconstruction (model.py:93) reaches encoder and decoder; F.mse_loss(x, x_q.detach()) (layers.py:178) reaches the encoder only. The codebook is deliberately not a gradient path: requires_grad_(False) at layers.py:84 keeps it out of AdamW's parameter list (train_rqvae.py:383-387) and it moves only through the detached scatter-add/exp_at step (frechet_poincare.py:170-199, model.py:78-80), which is exactly the sg the proposal specifies, so the absent codebook gradient is not a dead term. Nothing is computed and dropped: _last is consumed at model.py:53-62, the sums at model.py:75-80, item_weights at frechet_poincare.py:140, log_at/exp_at at :175/:194. Switch symmetry: use_behaviour False returns ones (:138-139); use_curvature False returns squared Euclidean distance and step (:145-151, :155-156, :174-177, :193-196), so the same path runs with either factor removed and the cost, slot and commitment all change. Numerics: clamp_ball keeps ||z|| <= 1-1e-4 (:42-53), every atanh argument is clamped to 1-1e-7 (:77, :84, :97-98), so the largest distance is 2*atanh(1-1e-7) ~ 16 with finite derivative; denominators use clamp_min(1e-12) (:39, :58, :69, :192); a non-finite slot is rejected at :197-199; the global clip (train_rqvae.py:445-446) bounds the amplified near-boundary gradient; a zero-norm tangent gives tanh(0)/(1e-12)=0 and log gives atanh(0)=0, so no 0/0. Loss finiteness is checked before backward (train_rqvae.py:442-443), and the step runs after optimizer.step() with the per-rank sums all-reduced first (train_rqvae.py:455-458), so the estimator cannot leave ranks with different codebooks.
FINDING SEVERITY: minor
FINDING LOCATION: model/frechet_poincare.py:156-157
FINDING DETAIL: in the Euclidean arm (use_curvature False) the commitment is the squared Euclidean distance between point = exp_0(latent), which is projected into the ball, and the ball-resident slot, while the Euclidean step at :196 re-clamps into the ball. The geometry-off arm is therefore a Euclidean metric on ball-projected points rather than the untouched Euclidean quantiser. This changes no computation of the trained both-on mechanism and no arm is trained with the switch off, so it is not blocking.
FINDING REPRODUCTION: set USE_GEOMETRY = False at train_rqvae.py:108 and read layers.py:153 with frechet_poincare.py:155-157 and :196.
FINDING CORRECTION: when use_curvature is False, compare and step on the raw latent (skip exp_0 in layers.py:153 and clamp_ball in frechet_poincare.py:196).

